## 4. Per-field metrics, aggregate strategy, and floors

Per DESIGN.md §7.1.1 metrics layer, this section carries an
aggregate-strategy block (one set across all fields), per-field
metric sub-blocks (one per OUTPUT_SCHEMA field), and per-field
floor sub-blocks (optional; zero or more). Under K=1 the section
collapses to one per-field metric sub-block, a trivial
aggregate-strategy block (any strategy is the identity), and at
most one floor sub-block — equivalent to v0.1.0's scalar fields.

**Aggregate strategy:**

- **`AGGREGATE_STRATEGY`:** {{AGGREGATE_STRATEGY}}
  <!-- one of {macro, weighted, min}; per metric-design SKILL.md
       §3.2 / DESIGN.md §7.1.1 metrics layer decision 2. Trivial
       under K=1 (any of the three is the identity on the lone
       field). -->
- **`AGGREGATE_WEIGHTS`:** {{AGGREGATE_WEIGHTS}}
  <!-- a vector of K non-negative weights summing to a documented
       constant (typically 1.0 or K); required when
       AGGREGATE_STRATEGY is `weighted`, absent otherwise. The
       weight order matches the per-field sub-blocks below. -->
- **`AGGREGATE_RATIONALE`:** {{AGGREGATE_RATIONALE}}
  <!-- one paragraph naming the §3.2 strawman path (homogeneity
       assessment, dimensional-mismatch revise signal, explicit
       weighting from task economics, etc.). Required regardless
       of strategy. Under K=1 a single sentence referencing the
       K=1 case is sufficient (e.g., "single-output classification;
       aggregate is identity on the lone field's metric"). -->

**Per-field metrics** (one sub-block per OUTPUT_SCHEMA field):

- **Field `{{FIELD_1_NAME}}`:**
  - `METRIC_NAME`: {{FIELD_1_METRIC_NAME}}
  - `METRIC_RATIONALE`: {{FIELD_1_METRIC_RATIONALE}}
  - `METRIC_INDEPENDENCE_NOTE`: {{FIELD_1_METRIC_INDEPENDENCE_NOTE}}
- **Field `{{FIELD_2_NAME}}`:**
  - `METRIC_NAME`: {{FIELD_2_METRIC_NAME}}
  - `METRIC_RATIONALE`: {{FIELD_2_METRIC_RATIONALE}}
  - `METRIC_INDEPENDENCE_NOTE`: {{FIELD_2_METRIC_INDEPENDENCE_NOTE}}
<!-- Add additional FIELD_N sub-blocks as needed; one per
     OUTPUT_SCHEMA field. METRIC_NAME[f] is one of the values
     listed in metric-design SKILL.md §6. METRIC_RATIONALE[f]
     names which §3.1 decision-tree branch (or which type-
     suggestion path) was taken and why, derived from the field's
     role in the task and from §3's DECISION_RULE / TRADEOFF_NOTES.
     METRIC_INDEPENDENCE_NOTE[f] confirms the metric is computable
     independently of the production model (DESIGN.md §5);
     multi-judge subjective metrics are forbidden in v1
     (DESIGN.md §7.1). The independence rule applies per field —
     one field's violation fails the rule for the task as a whole.
     Under K=1 there is one sub-block; the values are equivalent to
     v0.1.0's scalar METRIC_NAME / METRIC_RATIONALE /
     METRIC_INDEPENDENCE_NOTE. -->

**Per-field floors** (optional; one sub-block per field that
carries a floor; absent for fields without; the entire section may
be empty if no field carries a floor):

- **Field `{{FLOOR_FIELD_1_NAME}}`:**
  - `FLOOR`: {{FLOOR_FIELD_1_VALUE}}
  - `FLOOR_RATIONALE`: {{FLOOR_FIELD_1_RATIONALE}}
<!-- Add additional floor sub-blocks per field as needed. Floors
     are the exception, not the default; per metric-design SKILL.md
     §3.3, only fields the schema marks as required-and-
     unrecoverable typically carry a floor. The entire section may
     be empty (no sub-blocks below the heading) if the user
     declines floors for every field. Per-class-within-field floors
     are not a separate tier — define the field's primary metric
     to *be* the per-class metric (e.g., recall_on_class_X) per
