## 5. Model and lock-in posture

**Production model identifier:** `{{MODEL_IDENTIFIER}}`
<!-- MODEL_IDENTIFIER: the exact env-var string that the loop will
     use. No aliasing (DESIGN.md §2.2). E.g. "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18"
     or "qwen3-14b". -->

**Production model family:** {{MODEL_FAMILY}}
<!-- MODEL_FAMILY: the vendor/model family of MODEL_IDENTIFIER (e.g.
     anthropic, openai, google, meta). Default and recommended value:
     "auto" — the v0.7 cross-family gate resolves the family
     deterministically from MODEL_IDENTIFIER (scripts/_models.py;
     DESIGN.md §7.1.8). Set an explicit family ONLY when the model
     string is unrecognized by the resolver, which would otherwise hard-
     stop; an explicit value is the on-record fallback, never a way to
     override a recognized model. This field matters only when the v0.7
     `label-panel` sub-skill synthesizes baseline labels (see §6 Label
     synthesis): the Claude judge panel requires a non-Anthropic
     production model, so a Claude/Anthropic family hard-blocks the panel.
     It has no effect when labels are human-provided or already present. -->

**Lock-in posture:** {{LOCKIN_POSTURE}}
<!-- LOCKIN_POSTURE: one of {locked, multi-model-roadmap, exploring}.
     "locked" is the v1 default — the prompt is optimized for one
     model. v0.4 will support multi-model. "exploring" should be
     rare and triggers a warning that v1 cannot defend against model
     overfitting beyond documentation. -->

**Cross-model fragility plan:**
{{FRAGILITY_PLAN}}
<!-- FRAGILITY_PLAN: how the user will handle the prompt failing on
     other models if they ever swap. Acceptable answer: "we won't
     swap; if we do, we re-run /spp-loop against the new model."
     Becomes part of REPORT.md Limitations. -->

