## 6. Baseline

**Data source:** {{DATA_SOURCE}}
<!-- DATA_SOURCE: where rows come from (file, query, sampling
     procedure). Filled during consultation. -->

**Preprocess mapping:** {{PREPROCESS_MAPPING}}
<!-- PREPROCESS_MAPPING: how the raw data source maps to the canonical
     baseline.csv columns (id / input / label(s) / optional language),
     recorded by /spp-baseline step 4's `preprocess` sub-skill
     (sub-skills/preprocess/SKILL.md; DESIGN.md §7.1.7). Names which raw
     column became which canonical column, and how `language` was
     populated (user-supplied, or auto-detected via the on-demand
     language-ID library). Default for a data source already in
     canonical form: "identity (data already canonical)". Provenance for
     the deterministic preprocess.py; not the activation switch for any
     downstream behavior. -->

**Target baseline size:** {{BASELINE_TARGET_SIZE}} rows
<!-- BASELINE_TARGET_SIZE: typically 50–100 (DESIGN.md README "When
     to use this"). Stripped-scope plans may go smaller; document
     why if so. -->

**Class balance target:** {{CLASS_BALANCE_TARGET}}
<!-- CLASS_BALANCE_TARGET: e.g. "50/50 binary" or "preserve
     production prevalence." Affects stratified split. -->

**Language coverage:** {{LANGUAGE_COVERAGE}}
<!-- LANGUAGE_COVERAGE: the language make-up of the data and whether
     baseline.csv carries an optional per-row `language` column
     (BCP-47 tags, e.g. `en`, `es`, `zh-Hans`). Default and
     backward-compatible value: "monolingual" — no `language` column,
     and the runner behaves exactly as it did pre-v0.6. For
     multilingual data, list the languages and confirm the column is
     present, e.g. "multilingual: en, es, de (language column
     present)". The per-language machinery (per-language metric
     breakdown in §4 + language-stratified split in §7) auto-activates
     only when the column holds two or more distinct languages
     (DESIGN.md §7.1.7); it is data-driven, not a flag. Output labels
     stay canonical regardless of input language (§2). -->

**Label provenance:** {{LABEL_PROVENANCE}}
<!-- LABEL_PROVENANCE: who labels and how disagreements get
     resolved. Inputs to baseline-quality. -->

**Label synthesis:** {{LABEL_SYNTHESIS}}
<!-- LABEL_SYNTHESIS: whether the gold labels were synthesized by the
     v0.7 `label-panel` sub-skill (sub-skills/label-panel/SKILL.md;
     DESIGN.md §7.1.8) because the canonical baseline.csv arrived with no
     label column. Default value: "none (labels human-provided or already
     present)" — the panel did not run. When the panel synthesized labels,
     record the gate decision and panel configuration on the record: the
     production model's resolved family (which must differ from the
     Anthropic judge panel — the cross-family lock), the panel size and
     consensus rule, and the count of escalated rows the human
     adjudicated. E.g. "panel-synthesized: production family openai,
     5-judge / 4-of-5, 7 of 80 rows escalated and human-adjudicated". The
     judges decide against the §2 per-field definitions (the same rubric
     metric-design / schema-designer settle); labels freeze before the
     split and are never read by the scoring path (invariant #13). -->

**Status:** {{BASELINE_STATUS}}
<!-- BASELINE_STATUS: one of {not-started, in-progress, complete}.
     Updated by /spp-baseline; /spp-loop refuses to start if
     "complete" is not present. -->

