## 7. Splits

**Split ratios:** train {{TRAIN_PCT}}% / dev {{DEV_PCT}}% / test {{TEST_PCT}}%
<!-- TRAIN_PCT, DEV_PCT, TEST_PCT: integers summing to 100. Default
     60/20/20. Filled at gate G3 (split confirmation). -->

**Random seed:** {{SPLIT_SEED}}
<!-- SPLIT_SEED: integer. Reproducibility-critical. -->

**Stratification key:** {{STRATIFICATION_KEY}}
<!-- STRATIFICATION_KEY: usually the label column. Multi-class tasks
     may stratify on a derived key. When the data is multilingual
     (§6 Language coverage), the split also stratifies on `language`
     so every split — including the sacred test set — is
     representative of the language distribution; this is applied
     automatically in multilingual mode (DESIGN.md §7.1.7) and is a
     no-op otherwise. -->

**Sacred test set acknowledgment:** {{SACRED_TEST_ACK}}
<!-- SACRED_TEST_ACK: required value "acknowledged". Confirms the
     user understands the test set is not touched until Phase 3
     (DESIGN.md §10 glossary, sacred test set). Refusing this value
     is a refusal to use the methodology. -->

