## Validation rules

A `plan.md` is **correctly filled** when all of the following hold.
The Phase 4 template linter verifies these mechanically; the
designer agent verifies them at gate G1.

1. All `{{...}}` placeholders are resolved (no remaining `{{` or
   `}}` outside this validation list).
2. `TASK_NAME` is kebab-case, contains no spaces or slashes.
3. `OUTPUT_SCHEMA` passes the mechanical layer (per
   `schema-designer` SKILL.md §3.4: schema parses as JSON Schema
   draft 2020-12; every field has a `type`; every enum field's
   values are explicitly enumerated; required vs. optional is
   explicit; at least one example output validates; no `$ref`
   cycles; no naked `"type": "object"` without `"properties"` or
   `"additionalProperties": false`). Legacy v0.1.0 plans with
   `LABEL_SPACE` are auto-promoted by the runner's K=1 fallback.
4. `METRIC_NAME[f]` for each OUTPUT_SCHEMA field `f` is one of the
   allowed values listed in `metric-design` SKILL.md §6.
5. `METRIC_INDEPENDENCE_NOTE[f]` is present and non-empty for each
   OUTPUT_SCHEMA field; the rule's substance — independence-rule
   satisfaction per DESIGN.md §5; multi-judge subjective metrics
   forbidden in v1 (DESIGN.md §7.1) — is unchanged. A single
   field's empty or missing note fails this rule for the plan as a
   whole.
6. `MODEL_IDENTIFIER` is the exact env-var string with no aliasing
   (DESIGN.md §2.2).
7. `SACRED_TEST_ACK` literally equals `acknowledged`.
8. `AUDITOR_CONFIG` literally equals `per-iteration, no-score-access`
   (DESIGN.md §4.2 information-isolation lock).
9. `TRAIN_PCT + DEV_PCT + TEST_PCT == 100`.
10. `SPP_SCOPE` is one of the documented values; stripped scopes have
    a comment explaining what is skipped and why.
11. Every gate row in §9 has a non-empty `Approval phrase` cell.
12. The plan revision log has at least one row, with monotonically
    increasing `PLAN_VERSION` integers.
13. `LANGUAGE_COVERAGE` is present and non-empty. The default
    backward-compatible value is `monolingual`; a multilingual value
    names the languages and confirms the optional BCP-47 `language`
    column in `baseline.csv` (DESIGN.md §7.1.7). The per-language
    machinery is data-driven — it activates from the column's distinct-
    value count, not from this field — so this field is documentary
    intent, not the activation switch.
14. `PREPROCESS_MAPPING` is present and non-empty, recording how the raw
    data source maps to the canonical `baseline.csv` columns (or
    `identity (data already canonical)` when no mapping was needed),
    per `/spp-baseline` step 4 (DESIGN.md §7.1.7).
15. `MODEL_FAMILY` is present and non-empty. The default and recommended
    value is `auto` (the v0.7 cross-family gate resolves the family from
    `MODEL_IDENTIFIER`; DESIGN.md §7.1.8); an explicit family is required
    only when the resolver does not recognize the model string. An
    explicit value never overrides a recognized model.
16. `LABEL_SYNTHESIS` is present and non-empty. The default is
    `none (labels human-provided or already present)`; when the v0.7
    `label-panel` sub-skill synthesized labels, the value records the
    resolved production family (which must differ from the Anthropic judge
    panel), the panel size and consensus rule, and the human-adjudicated
    escalation count (DESIGN.md §7.1.8).
17. `TASK_MODE` is one of `classification` or `extraction`. The default
    backward-compatible value is `classification`; absent or unset reads as
    `classification` so every pre-v0.10 plan is unchanged (DESIGN.md
    §7.1.11). The value must be consistent with `OUTPUT_SCHEMA` (§2): the
    `schema-designer` sub-skill rejects a contradiction, e.g. `extraction`
    with a bare-enum schema or `classification` with an unbounded item-array
    schema.
